# Voyage capture — agent owns the reminder

Evan is not the day-to-day builder in this repo — **you are**. After you finish a **Marble Voyage / Plink build**, install, or playtest handoff, you must surface stage stills yourself. Do not wait for him to remember the script exists.

## Default (every major voyage build)

In the handoff message, include one short line:

> Stage stills available: `./scripts/build_marble_voyage.sh --capture` (or `--skip-build` if the `.app` is already built). Say the word and I’ll run it and open the PNGs.

Do **not** run capture automatically on every compile.

## When to actually capture

Run capture when Evan asks for stills / screenshots / “with capture” / layout review from the current build, or when you need PNGs to continue autonomous layout/art review:

```bash
./scripts/build_marble_voyage.sh --capture
# or, app already built:
./scripts/capture_marble_voyage.sh --skip-build
```

Then open `artifacts/voyage-capture/<stamp>/*.png` and review them.

## Interference

Capture relaunches the app on the capture simulator (default `iPad (A16)`). Prefer that dedicated sim; don’t yank a device Evan is actively playing. Reminder-only builds use `./scripts/build_marble_voyage.sh` with no `--capture`.

